        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d0c7fcca-69ac-5976-bc28-ec453fbc76ac",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mary Jane Phillips-Matz, Giuseppe Verdi, Antonio Ghislanzoni, Auguste Mariette, Temistocle Solera\n- Organizations: Columbia University, Smith College\n- Places: Lebanon, Ohio, Italy, United States, Busseto, Upper Manhattan, New York City\n- Works: Aida\n- Topics: Verdi research, opera authorship attribution, university background\n\nFacts:\n- Columbia University was established in 1754 and is a private Ivy League research university in Upper Manhattan, New York City.\n- Mary Jane Phillips-Matz was born in Lebanon, Ohio and was educated at Smith College and Columbia University.\n- Mary Jane Phillips-Matz lived for many years in Italy.\n- Mary Jane Phillips-Matz returned to the United States in the early 1970s.\n- After returning to the United States, Mary Jane Phillips-Matz spent her summers in Busseto, Giuseppe Verdi's hometown, where she continued extensive research on Verdi's life.\n- In discussing Aida, Mary Jane Phillips-Matz argued that the source behind Antonio Ghislanzoni's scheme was Temistocle Solera rather than the figure often credited, Auguste Mariette.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
